00:19:23.667 --> 00:19:24.577
- We have a long way to go.

00:19:24.577 --> 00:19:25.554
- We have a long way to go.

00:19:25.554 --> 00:19:27.177
We've been around a couple
hundred thousand years

00:19:27.177 --> 00:19:29.390
in our current anatomical form.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:30.990
Cro Magnon form.

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:33.590
And so, that means we
have a long way to go.

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:35.575
But this presumes that the species

00:19:35.575 --> 00:19:38.177
is not smart enough to kill itself.

00:19:38.177 --> 00:19:40.140
- Well, then it's over.

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:41.665
(laughter)

00:19:41.665 --> 00:19:43.367
It was nice knowing you guys.

00:19:43.367 --> 00:19:46.601
- Yeah, we have invented
multiple ways to kill ourselves.

00:19:46.601 --> 00:19:48.953
And I don't think the elephants did.

00:19:48.953 --> 00:19:50.517
Nobody else did this.

00:19:50.517 --> 00:19:52.077
The mice.

00:19:52.077 --> 00:19:53.876
No, they're not killing themselves.

00:19:53.876 --> 00:19:55.654
Humans, yes.

00:19:55.654 --> 00:19:58.627
- Yeah, maybe cockroaches
invented human beings.

00:19:58.627 --> 00:19:59.460
- [Neil] Why?

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.293
- 'Cause, when everything's gone,

00:20:00.293 --> 00:20:01.734
they're gonna be the only ones left.

00:20:01.734 --> 00:20:02.567
And it's like.

00:20:02.567 --> 00:20:03.400
- No, no, then they don't have to

00:20:03.400 --> 00:20:04.540
invent us in the first place.

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:06.153
What kind of reasoning are you using here?

00:20:06.153 --> 00:20:08.416
- They want everything else gone.

00:20:08.416 --> 00:20:09.690
- So, they need us to build the structures

00:20:09.690 --> 00:20:11.034
that they then move into.

00:20:11.034 --> 00:20:12.003
- Right, and they move in.

00:20:12.003 --> 00:20:14.254
(laughter)

00:20:14.254 --> 00:20:16.090
I don't mind it.

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:17.821
That makes perfect sense.

00:20:17.821 --> 00:20:19.254
We are.

00:20:19.254 --> 00:20:22.167
I think what he's really asking is,

00:20:22.167 --> 00:20:25.981
in your estimation,
from your sage opinion,

00:20:25.981 --> 00:20:29.627
how long do you think we will last?

00:20:29.627 --> 00:20:31.854
- I give us 20 years.

00:20:31.854 --> 00:20:34.104
(laughter)

00:20:36.398 --> 00:20:37.910
- [Chuck] Oh, that's funny.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:39.993
- No, I think we're good.

00:20:41.447 --> 00:20:43.210
This is why many people want to become

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:44.844
a two-planet species.

00:20:44.844 --> 00:20:45.874
Terraform Mars.

00:20:45.874 --> 00:20:47.158
Send some humans there.

00:20:47.158 --> 00:20:48.647
So, if something bad happens on Earth,

00:20:48.647 --> 00:20:50.784
you still have humans somewhere else.

00:20:50.784 --> 00:20:53.897
- Wow, that is not encouraging at all.

00:20:53.897 --> 00:20:55.623
- Not for half the people who
aren't on the planet that's.

00:20:55.623 --> 00:20:56.934
- Exactly.

00:20:56.934 --> 00:20:58.923
- So, if an asteroid
comes, if a killer virus,

00:20:58.923 --> 00:21:01.557
if AI gets out of hand.

00:21:01.557 --> 00:21:03.344
- So, I understand seeding something

00:21:03.344 --> 00:21:06.318
with a remnant for
survival of the species.

00:21:06.318 --> 00:21:07.680
That's extraneous.

00:21:07.680 --> 00:21:10.930
I mean, that's something that's outside

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:12.713
of our own destruction.

00:21:12.713 --> 00:21:16.057
Even though we could stop
an asteroid from hitting us

00:21:16.057 --> 00:21:16.890
if we put resources.

00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:18.319
- Ain't nobody doing it.

00:21:18.319 --> 00:21:19.152
But we know how.

00:21:19.152 --> 00:21:20.392
- [Chuck] I'm saying, if we
put the resources into it,

00:21:20.392 --> 00:21:21.880
we could stop even that from happening.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.130
- So, what's the example you're giving?

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.244
- What do you mean?

00:21:24.244 --> 00:21:25.293
To stop the asteroid?

00:21:25.293 --> 00:21:26.126
- No, no.

00:21:26.126 --> 00:21:30.459
- So, what I'm saying is
will we ever get to a place

00:21:32.279 --> 00:21:35.880
where, as the Buddhist monks call it,

00:21:35.880 --> 00:21:39.028
the so-called monkey brain that

00:21:39.028 --> 00:21:43.528
causes us to do so much
destructive work to each other

00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:48.020
and to the planet.

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:50.720
Will we ever get to a place
where we overcome that

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:54.170
or we're able to train
those who come behind us

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.894
to overcome that?

00:21:55.894 --> 00:21:58.994
Now, it does happen in some people.

00:21:58.994 --> 00:22:00.507
- I get it.

00:22:00.507 --> 00:22:02.610
First, I've never heard a Buddhist monk

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:05.224
say the phrase monkey brain.

00:22:05.224 --> 00:22:07.024
I've never heard that.

00:22:07.024 --> 00:22:07.857
This is a thing?

00:22:07.857 --> 00:22:08.690
- This is a thing.

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:09.523
- Okay, fine.

00:22:09.523 --> 00:22:11.034
I got to attend more monasteries.

00:22:11.034 --> 00:22:13.334
You feeling monkey brain today?

00:22:13.334 --> 00:22:14.397
All right.

00:22:14.397 --> 00:22:15.384
- Delicious.

00:22:15.384 --> 00:22:16.760
- I've heard of reptilian brain.

00:22:16.760 --> 00:22:17.659
But not monkey brain.

00:22:17.659 --> 00:22:22.434
So, the reptilian brain
reference something primal

00:22:22.434 --> 00:22:24.173
that goes on within you.

00:22:24.173 --> 00:22:26.124
So, if we follow the
reasoning by Steven Pinker

00:22:26.124 --> 00:22:28.647
in his book The Better
Angels of Our Nature,

00:22:28.647 --> 00:22:31.772
he studied the likelihood of
you dying before maturity,

00:22:31.772 --> 00:22:35.747
or dying before adulthood, which is dying,

00:22:35.747 --> 00:22:37.997
at the hands of another human

00:22:37.997 --> 00:22:41.885
from early days of tribal
warfare to modern days

00:22:41.885 --> 00:22:44.802
of state-sanctioned global warfare.

00:22:48.747 --> 00:22:50.887
And what he found is that the likelihood

00:22:50.887 --> 00:22:54.174
of you dying in that way has
been dropping ever since.

00:22:54.174 --> 00:22:55.047
- Okay.

00:22:55.047 --> 00:22:58.287
- So, tribal warfare, you would
kill maybe a third or half

00:22:58.287 --> 00:22:59.987
of the other tribe.

00:22:59.987 --> 00:23:01.922
Or the entire tribe.

00:23:01.922 --> 00:23:03.960
And then you win and you get their land.

00:23:03.960 --> 00:23:04.997
That doesn't happen today.

00:23:04.997 --> 00:23:05.830
- True.

00:23:06.770 --> 00:23:09.760
- [Neil] The state surrenders
before that happens.

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:10.593
- True.

00:23:10.593 --> 00:23:12.647
- Saving the lives of the
rest of the population.

00:23:12.647 --> 00:23:13.480
If you look at.

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:14.487
I did this just recently.

00:23:14.487 --> 00:23:16.487
If you look at what countries had

00:23:16.487 --> 00:23:19.310
the greatest percent
of their population die

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:21.060
in the Second World War.

00:23:21.060 --> 00:23:22.421
Was it Belarus?

00:23:22.421 --> 00:23:23.260
One of them is very high.

00:23:23.260 --> 00:23:24.360
It's like a third.

00:23:24.360 --> 00:23:25.474
I forgot the exact numbers.

00:23:25.474 --> 00:23:26.647
But they're high.

00:23:26.647 --> 00:23:28.087
But they're not half.

00:23:28.087 --> 00:23:29.674
And you keep going down.

00:23:29.674 --> 00:23:32.787
And you get to even Germany.

00:23:32.787 --> 00:23:34.309
Even ones that were heavily bombed.

00:23:34.309 --> 00:23:35.559
Germany, Japan.

00:23:36.884 --> 00:23:39.447
A fraction of the total population.

00:23:39.447 --> 00:23:42.360
That is not how it used
to end in tribal warfare.

00:23:42.360 --> 00:23:47.360
So, now consider that, even so,
during the Second World War,

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:51.284
between 1939 and 1945,

00:23:51.284 --> 00:23:55.367
1,000 humans were killed
by other humans per hour

00:23:57.297 --> 00:24:00.268
for every hour from 1939 to 1945.

00:24:00.268 --> 00:24:01.684
- Wow.

00:24:01.684 --> 00:24:02.517
- [Neil] Is that going on today?

00:24:02.517 --> 00:24:04.110
No, no.

00:24:04.110 --> 00:24:05.918
- No, we're really slipping.

00:24:05.918 --> 00:24:07.210
- No, stop.

00:24:07.210 --> 00:24:09.070
- We really gotta pick up our game.

00:24:09.070 --> 00:24:09.903
- Just so we can.

00:24:09.903 --> 00:24:11.320
So, the point is.

00:24:13.147 --> 00:24:15.734
Often, that era is called
The Greatest Generation.

00:24:15.734 --> 00:24:20.418
'Cause they fought evil
forces and this sort of thing.

00:24:20.418 --> 00:24:23.345
Although my father fought
in a segregated Army.

00:24:23.345 --> 00:24:25.397
So, he's not thinking that
was the greatest generation.

00:24:25.397 --> 00:24:29.520
He has other perspectives on that period.

00:24:29.520 --> 00:24:31.508
- [Chuck] It's the second
greatest generation.

00:24:31.508 --> 00:24:34.357
- My point is is the greatest generation

00:24:34.357 --> 00:24:36.334
the one where the fewest fraction

00:24:36.334 --> 00:24:39.020
of everyone dies out of hate?

00:24:39.020 --> 00:24:40.284
We might have a lot of hate.

00:24:40.284 --> 00:24:42.134
But, if the number of
people who die from it

00:24:42.134 --> 00:24:43.960
is lower than ever before,

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:46.747
then this arc that you are hinting at,

00:24:46.747 --> 00:24:49.910
that maybe the next generation
learns from the previous one,

00:24:49.910 --> 00:24:51.910
maybe that's gonna work.

00:24:52.760 --> 00:24:55.368
Europe, with all of their
turbulence and turmoil,

00:24:55.368 --> 00:24:56.710
they actually haven't been at war

00:24:56.710 --> 00:24:58.960
with each other for 70 years.

00:24:58.960 --> 00:25:00.420
Is there another 70 year period

00:25:00.420 --> 00:25:03.970
in the history of Europe where
nobody was fighting anybody?

00:25:03.970 --> 00:25:05.560
I don't think so.

00:25:05.560 --> 00:25:07.446
- Not if Twitter has
anything to do with it.

00:25:07.446 --> 00:25:09.834
(laughter)

00:25:09.834 --> 00:25:12.370
- What you're saying is
imagine if Twitter existed.

00:25:12.370 --> 00:25:13.203
- [Chuck] Back then.

00:25:13.203 --> 00:25:14.036
- Back then.

00:25:14.036 --> 00:25:14.869
Oh my gosh.

00:25:14.869 --> 00:25:15.702
- Let me tell you something.

00:25:15.702 --> 00:25:19.546
The war wouldn't have stopped
until everybody was dead.

00:25:19.546 --> 00:25:22.384
People would have said, "I surrender."

00:25:22.384 --> 00:25:23.746
A tweet would have gone out.

00:25:23.746 --> 00:25:25.432
It would be like, "I take it back.

00:25:25.432 --> 00:25:26.647
Let's keep fighting.

00:25:26.647 --> 00:25:27.884
Let's keep fighting.

00:25:27.884 --> 00:25:28.810
I don't care."

00:25:28.810 --> 00:25:30.910
- I hate you more.

00:25:30.910 --> 00:25:34.577
So, maybe we are getting
kinder and gentler.

00:25:35.734 --> 00:25:37.810
Time still needs to bear that out

00:25:37.810 --> 00:25:39.847
on a level that would please everyone.

00:25:39.847 --> 00:25:42.347
But I still worry that this primal brain

00:25:42.347 --> 00:25:47.110
will always segregate us all
by some arbitrary factor.

00:25:47.110 --> 00:25:49.534
And thereby justify doing
harm to other groups.

00:25:49.534 --> 00:25:51.044
- Interesting.

00:25:51.044 --> 00:25:52.510
I think you're right.

00:25:52.510 --> 00:25:53.531
- Who's the comedian?

00:25:53.531 --> 00:25:55.417
Was it Franklin Ajaye?

00:25:55.417 --> 00:25:56.584
One of the guys from the '70s.

00:25:56.584 --> 00:25:57.417
- Back in the day.

00:25:57.417 --> 00:25:58.250
- In the day.

00:25:58.250 --> 00:25:59.184
In the day.

00:25:59.184 --> 00:26:02.070
He was talking about who
hates who in the world.

00:26:02.070 --> 00:26:04.570
And he says, "Read the papers?

00:26:07.734 --> 00:26:08.567
What?

00:26:09.437 --> 00:26:13.937
In Northern Ireland, the
Protestants and the Catholics

00:26:14.837 --> 00:26:16.286
are fighting each other?

00:26:16.286 --> 00:26:17.884
And they're both white?"

00:26:17.884 --> 00:26:19.360
He said, "You know I don't have a chance.

00:26:19.360 --> 00:26:20.674
'Cause I'm Black."

00:26:20.674 --> 00:26:21.507
- That's funny.

00:26:21.507 --> 00:26:22.340
That's true.

00:26:22.340 --> 00:26:25.260
- If white people divide
themselves up in that way,

00:26:25.260 --> 00:26:27.574
two Christian communities
killing each other

00:26:27.574 --> 00:26:29.684
and they're both white and
they're both Christian.

00:26:29.684 --> 00:26:31.110
- It's over for you, brother.

00:26:31.110 --> 00:26:32.774
- It's over for everybody else.

00:26:32.774 --> 00:26:35.046
If people can kill each
other for those reasons,

00:26:35.046 --> 00:26:37.210
it's almost no hope in this world.

00:26:37.210 --> 00:26:39.924
So, yeah, I don't know.

00:26:39.924 --> 00:26:40.774
So, I'm sorry.

00:26:40.774 --> 00:26:41.947
I don't have a good answer.

00:26:41.947 --> 00:26:43.374
- That was a pretty good answer.

00:26:43.374 --> 00:26:45.074
The answer is we're not gonna make it.

00:26:45.074 --> 00:26:47.110
(laughter)

00:26:47.110 --> 00:26:48.023
- I'd like to think we go

00:26:48.023 --> 00:26:49.147
thousands of years into the future

00:26:49.147 --> 00:26:50.760
and possibly outlive the sun.

00:26:50.760 --> 00:26:52.224
- [Chuck] All right, that'd be great.

00:26:52.224 --> 00:26:55.371
- But starhopping to
other planetary systems.

00:26:55.371 --> 00:26:56.610
- That's, you know, I'm just gonna say

00:26:56.610 --> 00:26:57.747
that's the way it's gonna end.

00:26:57.747 --> 00:26:58.580
'Cause I won't be here.

00:26:58.580 --> 00:26:59.424
So, that's great.

00:26:59.424 --> 00:27:00.709
- Maybe.

00:27:00.709 --> 00:27:04.210
It has been said that the
first person who will never die

00:27:04.210 --> 00:27:05.237
is now alive.

00:27:05.237 --> 00:27:06.070
- What?

00:27:07.174 --> 00:27:08.007
That's a.

00:27:08.007 --> 00:27:09.324
- No, this is how you do it.

00:27:09.324 --> 00:27:10.287
- [Chuck] I know what you're saying.

00:27:10.287 --> 00:27:11.660
- So, they get some new thing that

00:27:11.660 --> 00:27:13.510
makes you live an extra 50 years.

00:27:13.510 --> 00:27:15.672
So, now you live to 150 instead of 100.

00:27:15.672 --> 00:27:19.271
And then, somewhere in
there is another thing.

00:27:19.271 --> 00:27:21.158
Now, you can live another 200 years.

00:27:21.158 --> 00:27:23.174
So, now the 150 goes to 350.

00:27:23.174 --> 00:27:24.497
Now you can live 500 years.

00:27:24.497 --> 00:27:25.822
Now you go to 1000.

00:27:25.822 --> 00:27:27.047
You can live 5000 years now.

00:27:27.047 --> 00:27:32.047
So, as we progress in our
understanding of what ages you.

00:27:32.487 --> 00:27:35.260
If we can reverse that or
prevent it from ever advancing,

00:27:35.260 --> 00:27:38.324
there's someone alive today
who will benefit from this.

00:27:38.324 --> 00:27:39.360
- That's pretty cool.

00:27:39.360 --> 00:27:40.193
I like it.

00:27:40.193 --> 00:27:42.737
- So, if that happens, you
better find another planet.

00:27:42.737 --> 00:27:43.570
That's all.

00:27:43.570 --> 00:27:44.403
- This is true.

00:27:44.403 --> 00:27:46.560
That's the premise of a
show called Altered Carbon.

00:27:46.560 --> 00:27:49.237
Where people actually
take their consciousness

00:27:49.237 --> 00:27:52.474
and put it into what they call
a sleeve, which is the body.

00:27:52.474 --> 00:27:55.937
- I think I voiceovered the
opening sequence to that show.

00:27:55.937 --> 00:27:56.770
- Oh my god.

00:27:56.770 --> 00:27:57.837
I think we had that conversation once

00:27:57.837 --> 00:27:58.670
where you told me that.

00:27:58.670 --> 00:27:59.787
'Cause I told you I was a fan.

00:27:59.787 --> 00:28:01.709
- I don't remember if it was
the pilot or the other shows.

00:28:01.709 --> 00:28:04.558
But I lent my voice to the cause.

00:28:04.558 --> 00:28:05.997
- Nice.

00:28:05.997 --> 00:28:07.184
Wow, all right.

00:28:07.184 --> 00:28:08.810
Well, let's go to joey24.

00:28:08.810 --> 00:28:09.643
Joeyjr24.

00:28:10.724 --> 00:28:12.674
He says this personal question.

00:28:12.674 --> 00:28:16.184
Based on all your experiences
and knowledge thus far.

00:28:16.184 --> 00:28:17.474
- Personal for me or for you?

00:28:17.474 --> 00:28:18.410
- [Chuck] Personal for you.

00:28:18.410 --> 00:28:19.243
- Okay.

00:28:19.243 --> 00:28:20.397
- Nobody asking me anything.

00:28:20.397 --> 00:28:23.134
