00:28:45.797 --> 00:28:46.630
- I was gonna say.

00:28:46.630 --> 00:28:47.634
Here's the meaning of life right now.

00:28:47.634 --> 00:28:49.947
Plug your book when you get a chance.

00:28:49.947 --> 00:28:52.360
(laughter)

00:28:52.360 --> 00:28:54.258
- My next book's called
Letters From an Astrophysicist.

00:28:54.258 --> 00:28:55.091
- [Chuck] You know what?

00:28:55.091 --> 00:28:55.924
Yes.

00:28:55.924 --> 00:28:56.897
- It's the correspondence
I've had with people

00:28:56.897 --> 00:29:00.814
who've had similar angst
about their existence.

00:29:02.131 --> 00:29:03.107
- That's not just the book.

00:29:03.107 --> 00:29:04.184
It's not about that.

00:29:04.184 --> 00:29:06.024
It's about all kind of different
letters you've received.

00:29:06.024 --> 00:29:07.267
- All kinds of letters.

00:29:07.267 --> 00:29:09.607
But a very recurring theme is that

00:29:09.607 --> 00:29:12.280
people want to know the meaning of life

00:29:12.280 --> 00:29:14.994
and the significance of
their life in this world.

00:29:14.994 --> 00:29:16.717
And some of them come
from religious angles.

00:29:16.717 --> 00:29:17.594
Some are secular.

00:29:17.594 --> 00:29:20.044
But everybody's got this burning issue.

00:29:20.044 --> 00:29:20.877
- Yes.

00:29:20.877 --> 00:29:23.380
- So, here's how I have dealt with it.

00:29:23.380 --> 00:29:24.457
Others will do it other ways.

00:29:24.457 --> 00:29:25.290
- [Chuck] Okay.

00:29:25.290 --> 00:29:26.123
- But here's how I deal with it.

00:29:26.123 --> 00:29:26.956
- [Chuck] I'm interested now.

00:29:26.956 --> 00:29:29.817
- Many people are in search
of the meaning of life

00:29:29.817 --> 00:29:33.567
as though it's behind
a tree or under a rock.

00:29:35.444 --> 00:29:37.842
- Everybody knows it's in a drawer.

00:29:37.842 --> 00:29:40.824
- In the back near the paperclip.

00:29:40.824 --> 00:29:42.580
- It's in that junk drawer, too.

00:29:42.580 --> 00:29:44.744
It's not like an underwear
drawer or something.

00:29:44.744 --> 00:29:45.577
You know that drawer.

00:29:45.577 --> 00:29:47.684
You go to look for stamps and stuff.

00:29:47.684 --> 00:29:48.784
- Yeah, yeah, that drawer.

00:29:48.784 --> 00:29:49.617
That drawer.

00:29:49.617 --> 00:29:50.450
The junk drawer.

00:29:50.450 --> 00:29:51.283
- The junk drawer.

00:29:51.283 --> 00:29:52.116
- Everybody's got a junk drawer.

00:29:52.116 --> 00:29:52.949
- Everybody got a junk drawer.

00:29:52.949 --> 00:29:53.782
- It's near the kitchen somewhere.

00:29:53.782 --> 00:29:56.699
So, if you are looking for meaning,

00:29:59.407 --> 00:30:01.719
you may never find it.

00:30:01.719 --> 00:30:05.552
So, instead, recognize
that you have the power

00:30:06.667 --> 00:30:08.584
to manufacture meaning.

00:30:09.630 --> 00:30:11.945
Create it within yourself.

00:30:11.945 --> 00:30:13.717
And that's what I do.

00:30:13.717 --> 00:30:18.717
My meaning for life is derived
by several simple principles.

00:30:20.166 --> 00:30:23.780
Have I lessened the
sufferings of others today?

00:30:23.780 --> 00:30:26.057
That brings meaning to me.

00:30:26.057 --> 00:30:29.230
Because that means the
world is a little better off

00:30:29.230 --> 00:30:31.730
because I was in it today.

00:30:31.730 --> 00:30:35.994
If, after your day is over,
the world is worse off,

00:30:35.994 --> 00:30:37.743
you have subtracted meaning.

00:30:37.743 --> 00:30:40.080
- I should kill myself.

00:30:40.080 --> 00:30:42.424
'Cause, at the end of every day,

00:30:42.424 --> 00:30:45.841
somebody is like "That mother beep beep."

00:30:47.987 --> 00:30:49.437
But go ahead.

00:30:49.437 --> 00:30:53.520
- So, lessen the suffering
of others in some way.

00:30:55.021 --> 00:30:55.854
It doesn't mean redirect

00:30:55.854 --> 00:30:57.410
your whole life, mind, body, and soul.

00:30:57.410 --> 00:30:59.548
But, if you can help
someone across the street,

00:30:59.548 --> 00:31:03.548
help an aging person,
make a little child laugh.

00:31:04.899 --> 00:31:07.547
Just put a little bit of joy in the world

00:31:07.547 --> 00:31:08.585
to lessen the suffering.

00:31:08.585 --> 00:31:10.260
I also try to learn something every day.

00:31:10.260 --> 00:31:11.472
- All right.

00:31:11.472 --> 00:31:14.805
- Now, I like being a perpetual student.

00:31:16.037 --> 00:31:18.400
Most people hated being students.

00:31:18.400 --> 00:31:20.260
This saddens me.

00:31:20.260 --> 00:31:22.060
School is finished and what do you do?

00:31:22.060 --> 00:31:23.237
You run down the steps.

00:31:23.237 --> 00:31:26.224
♪ School is out forever.♪

00:31:26.224 --> 00:31:27.110
Out for the summer.

00:31:27.110 --> 00:31:30.352
That attitude captured in that song

00:31:30.352 --> 00:31:34.109
is as though you don't
want to be in school.

00:31:34.109 --> 00:31:36.559
And what's your only job in school?

00:31:36.559 --> 00:31:37.392
- It's to learn.

00:31:37.392 --> 00:31:38.225
- To learn.

00:31:38.225 --> 00:31:40.449
And somehow that's a chore.

00:31:40.449 --> 00:31:42.383
I don't blame you for feeling that way.

00:31:42.383 --> 00:31:44.574
I blame the school system

00:31:44.574 --> 00:31:48.049
for not instilling within
us eternal curiosity.

00:31:48.049 --> 00:31:50.313
Knowing that you'll spend
more years of your life

00:31:50.313 --> 00:31:51.799
not in school than in school.

00:31:51.799 --> 00:31:53.586
And so, if you have curiosity,

00:31:53.586 --> 00:31:55.176
you can be a lifelong learner.

00:31:55.176 --> 00:31:58.576
And so, I want to lessen
the sufferings of others

00:31:58.576 --> 00:32:00.236
and make sure I learn something more

00:32:00.236 --> 00:32:03.111
about the world today
than I did yesterday.

00:32:03.111 --> 00:32:03.944
- Nice.

00:32:03.944 --> 00:32:06.149
- And who's to say whether that
extra increment of learning

00:32:06.149 --> 00:32:11.149
can help me be better at lessening
the sufferings of others?

00:32:12.876 --> 00:32:15.013
So, that is how I make meaning in life.

00:32:15.013 --> 00:32:17.426
And, as a result, I've
owned thousands of books.

00:32:17.426 --> 00:32:18.663
Thousands.

00:32:18.663 --> 00:32:20.624
And I read a little bit.

00:32:20.624 --> 00:32:21.836
You know, I have a
little stash near my bed

00:32:21.836 --> 00:32:23.362
and I cycle them out.

00:32:23.362 --> 00:32:25.649
And, every day, I try.

00:32:25.649 --> 00:32:26.482
It's harder now.

00:32:26.482 --> 00:32:27.613
'Cause I get recognized.

00:32:27.613 --> 00:32:30.463
But I try to help people every day.

00:32:30.463 --> 00:32:31.313
Total strangers.

00:32:31.313 --> 00:32:32.436
- That's nice.

00:32:32.436 --> 00:32:34.699
- Yeah, so, you can make
meaning for yourself.

00:32:34.699 --> 00:32:35.626
Don't look for it.

00:32:35.626 --> 00:32:37.136
'Cause you may never find it.

00:32:37.136 --> 00:32:38.426
- You know, I'm gonna say.

00:32:38.426 --> 00:32:41.259
As a philosophy, that's admirable.

00:32:42.749 --> 00:32:43.582
That's doable.

00:32:43.582 --> 00:32:44.415
- [Neil] That's in the book.

00:32:44.415 --> 00:32:45.248
I wrote that in the book.

00:32:45.248 --> 00:32:46.081
- Nice, excellent, excellent.

00:32:46.081 --> 00:32:47.086
- Thank you.

00:32:47.086 --> 00:32:47.979
Give me another question.

00:32:47.979 --> 00:32:48.874
- We got one more question coming.

00:32:48.874 --> 00:32:49.749
- We can fit it in this segment.

00:32:49.749 --> 00:32:50.949
Go on.

00:32:50.949 --> 00:32:52.086
- Oh, here we go.

00:32:52.086 --> 00:32:52.919
Aw, man.

00:32:52.919 --> 00:32:53.752
- What?

00:32:53.752 --> 00:32:55.502
- Ninjanay, ninjanay.

00:32:56.762 --> 00:32:58.624
Okay, there you go.

00:32:58.624 --> 00:33:00.163
