00:33:01.663 --> 00:33:03.536
Damn you, people.

00:33:03.536 --> 00:33:04.369
- Okay.

00:33:04.369 --> 00:33:08.286
- On Instagram, says "I
keep hearing the phrase

00:33:11.499 --> 00:33:13.166
the vacuum of space.

00:33:15.476 --> 00:33:18.253
How exactly is it a vacuum?"

00:33:18.253 --> 00:33:19.263
- [Neil] Very nice.

00:33:19.263 --> 00:33:20.799
- That's a really good question.

00:33:20.799 --> 00:33:22.258
- Okay, so, when I was a kid,

00:33:22.258 --> 00:33:23.746
a vacuum was a physical object.

00:33:23.746 --> 00:33:24.579
- Yes, it was.

00:33:24.579 --> 00:33:26.546
- When I heard physicists
speak of the vacuum of space,

00:33:26.546 --> 00:33:29.883
I just imagined all
these Hoovers in the sky.

00:33:29.883 --> 00:33:32.059
So, I didn't know that
a vacuum was a thing.

00:33:32.059 --> 00:33:34.283
It was a concept.

00:33:34.283 --> 00:33:37.319
And then you make a machine
that duplicates that thing.

00:33:37.319 --> 00:33:38.759
I just didn't know that.

00:33:38.759 --> 00:33:39.609
So, I learned.

00:33:39.609 --> 00:33:44.609
Okay, so, a vacuum is where
there's basically no air.

00:33:44.633 --> 00:33:47.246
Okay, you can have objects there.

00:33:47.246 --> 00:33:48.346
But, when we think of a vacuum,

00:33:48.346 --> 00:33:50.219
it's not a place where
there isn't anything.

00:33:50.219 --> 00:33:51.052
It's a place where there's

00:33:51.052 --> 00:33:53.496
no air molecules moving typically.

00:33:53.496 --> 00:33:56.209
Generally, you can have some.

00:33:56.209 --> 00:33:59.083
And we would still
classify it as a vacuum.

00:33:59.083 --> 00:34:00.759
You have to distinguish
a regular, old vacuum

00:34:00.759 --> 00:34:02.683
or a perfect vacuum.

00:34:02.683 --> 00:34:03.516
You know what happens?

00:34:03.516 --> 00:34:04.349
If there's an object

00:34:04.349 --> 00:34:05.819
and you take away all the air molecules,

00:34:05.819 --> 00:34:07.569
the object outgasses.

00:34:08.432 --> 00:34:10.433
There are air molecules embedded

00:34:10.433 --> 00:34:11.959
in the surface of that object

00:34:11.959 --> 00:34:12.946
and they start coming out.

00:34:12.946 --> 00:34:13.779
It's fascinating.

00:34:13.779 --> 00:34:14.612
Then you heat it.

00:34:14.612 --> 00:34:15.483
It sends out more.

00:34:15.483 --> 00:34:17.683
It's very hard to make a perfect vacuum.

00:34:17.683 --> 00:34:18.883
Very hard.

00:34:18.883 --> 00:34:20.658
So, here's an old saying.

00:34:20.658 --> 00:34:21.491
Nature.

00:34:23.343 --> 00:34:25.146
- Abhors a vacuum.

00:34:25.146 --> 00:34:25.979
- Abhors a vacuum.

00:34:25.979 --> 00:34:27.559
These are people who have
never been into space.

00:34:27.559 --> 00:34:28.717
Most of the universe is a vacuum.

00:34:28.717 --> 00:34:31.133
Nature loves a vacuum.

00:34:31.133 --> 00:34:32.369
- [Chuck] Nice.

00:34:32.369 --> 00:34:33.533
- Was I Trumpy in there.

00:34:33.533 --> 00:34:34.446
Love.

00:34:34.446 --> 00:34:36.446
- Nature loves a vacuum.

00:34:37.833 --> 00:34:38.750
- A vacuum.

00:34:40.233 --> 00:34:43.146
- Preferably Trump brand vacuums.

00:34:43.146 --> 00:34:44.813
Trump brand vacuums.

00:34:45.746 --> 00:34:47.083
We suck the best.

00:34:47.083 --> 00:34:49.933
(laughter)

00:34:49.933 --> 00:34:50.881
- There's another saying.

00:34:50.881 --> 00:34:52.109
There's no such thing as gravity.

00:34:52.109 --> 00:34:52.942
Earth sucks.

00:34:52.942 --> 00:34:53.775
You ever hear that one?

00:34:53.775 --> 00:34:54.608
- Oh, okay.

00:34:54.608 --> 00:34:56.596
- So, the point is, when
there's a source of gravity,

00:34:56.596 --> 00:34:59.494
all the air wants to go
to that source of gravity.

00:34:59.494 --> 00:35:02.123
And it leaves a vacuum everywhere else.

00:35:02.123 --> 00:35:04.896
So, a vacuum is simply
where there's no air.

00:35:04.896 --> 00:35:06.570
And it's not anything deep.

00:35:06.570 --> 00:35:08.173
The odd thing in the universe is that

00:35:08.173 --> 00:35:11.959
you have places where
gas molecules collect.

00:35:11.959 --> 00:35:15.023
Those are the unusual
places in the universe.

00:35:15.023 --> 00:35:16.671
And they're called stars
and gaseous planets

00:35:16.671 --> 00:35:19.609
and the atmospheres of rocky planets.

00:35:19.609 --> 00:35:20.609
- [Chuck] Nice.

00:35:20.609 --> 00:35:21.482
- So, there you have a vacuum.

00:35:21.482 --> 00:35:23.223
So, Chuck, I want to put some closure

00:35:23.223 --> 00:35:24.473
on this vacuum question.

00:35:24.473 --> 00:35:25.306
- Okay.

00:35:25.306 --> 00:35:26.259
- Okay, this is the second.

00:35:26.259 --> 00:35:27.959
No, the third book I ever published.

00:35:27.959 --> 00:35:28.792
- Oh, okay.

00:35:28.792 --> 00:35:29.996
- It's called Just Visiting This Planet.

00:35:29.996 --> 00:35:30.829
